From 0c2aaa3023ea749ec139492bc212002252d2eb22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lu-Fi <lu-fi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:21:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sensor: t23 sc2336, apply shvflip before stream-on, not after

sensor_init() wrote the mode table (ending on stream-on, 0x0100=0x01),
then made a separate I2C read+write to 0x3221 for shvflip - right
after the sensor had just been told to start streaming. That
intermittently NAK'd (-EIO), leaving boards with shvflip=1 running
un-mirrored on the affected boot (reported: Galayou Y4, T23/sc2336).

Move stream-on out of the mode table (reusing the existing
sensor_stream_on_mipi[] that sensor_s_stream() already has) and do it
after the shvflip write instead of before, so the flip register access
happens on an idle bus.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 common/sensor/t23/sc2336.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/common/sensor/t23/sc2336.c b/common/sensor/t23/sc2336.c
index 0acd08ce..1cc0e756 100644
--- a/common/sensor/t23/sc2336.c
+++ b/common/sensor/t23/sc2336.c
@@ -468,7 +468,6 @@ static struct regval_list sensor_init_regs_1920_1080_30fps_mipi[] = {
 	{0x5aff, 0x28},
 	{0x36e9, 0x53},
 	{0x37f9, 0x53},
-	{0x0100, 0x01},
 	{SENSOR_REG_END, 0x00},
 };
 
@@ -700,8 +699,12 @@ static int sensor_init(struct tx_isp_subdev *sd, int enable) {
 	 * from the first frame, independent of which ISP tuning API (if
 	 * any) a given streamer calls. Must run after the mode table above
 	 * (register 0x0103 in that table resets the sensor and would wipe
-	 * this) and is safe to fail softly - a write error here shouldn't
-	 * block streaming, just leave the image un-mirrored.
+	 * this) and before stream-on below: this register access intermittently
+	 * NAK'd (-EIO) when it ran right after the sensor had just been told to
+	 * start streaming (mode table used to end on 0x0100=0x01 itself), most
+	 * likely too little settle time after that command for another I2C
+	 * transaction. Failing here is still soft - an error just leaves the
+	 * image un-mirrored, same as before.
 	 */
 	if (shvflip) {
 		ret = sensor_set_vflip(sd, 3);
@@ -709,6 +712,11 @@ static int sensor_init(struct tx_isp_subdev *sd, int enable) {
 			ISP_ERROR("%s: failed to apply shvflip (%d)\n", __func__, ret);
 	}
 
+	ret = sensor_write_array(sd, sensor_stream_on_mipi);
+	if (ret) {
+		return ret;
+	}
+
 	ret = tx_isp_call_subdev_notify(sd, TX_ISP_EVENT_SYNC_SENSOR_ATTR, &sensor->video);
 	sensor->priv = wsize;
 
